-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/FIV> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "Rhyolitic and dacitic lavas, basaltic pillow lavas. Spilitic breccias, acid tuffs and intercalated volcaniclastic sediments. (Correlative of Fishguard Volcanic Group-Llanrian Volcanic Group."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/GFT> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Conformably overlies the felsic Gwern Feifod Lava Member [Llangynog Formation]."@en .
-<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/LGF> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLowerBoundaryDefinition> "Supposedly unconformable on mudstones of the Craig-y-gln Group [Oswestry Sheet 137]."@en .
